7 true] [17592186306709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534737 true] [17592186306709 1100 "A mail truck departs from the post office at the origin and drives with a constant velocity of $(4i-3j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the truck to the origin after $2$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306709 1113 #uuid "f61b77d9-5a00-5a3c-a675-ee9a1e23e376" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306709 1145 "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i-3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the truck after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(4i-3j)(2) \\\\  & =(8i-6j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the truck to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|8i-6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306711 13194139534737 true] [17592186306710 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534737 true] [17592186306710 1041 "field-1" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306710 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306711 13194139534737 true] [17592186306710 1110 #uuid "0677a7e7-8aaf-51da-832a-2aa3fbf65e47" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306711 1034 "10" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534737 true] [17592186306711 1111 #uuid "12911a5a-e222-56dc-b1f7-1b1e980b6901" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306713 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1089 "q-280531" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1100 "A car accelerates from rest at the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1113 #uuid "f056a195-eb0d-534f-b5c8-1e1d2056a427" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306712 1145 "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i,\\,a=3i-4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the car after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(3i-4j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =8i+8(3i-4j) \\\\  & =8i+24i-32j \\\\  & =(32i-32j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the car to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|32i-32j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(32)^{2}+(-32)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1024+1024} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2048} \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306714 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306715 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1041 "field-1" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306715 13194139534737 true] [17592186306713 1110 #uuid "c555a797-9f97-5397-8b50-54d365a7a1e5" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306714 1034 "32" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534737 true] [17592186306714 1111 #uuid "65000e70-f9cc-5587-8d3d-34588f51716a" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306715 1034 "32\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534737 true] [17592186306715 1111 #uuid "76eebddb-3d5f-5409-b754-79172fe50441" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306717 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1089 "q-280535" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1100 "A cyclist begins at the position $(2i-j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the cyclist to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1113 #uuid "fd7864c9-0a89-5e68-91c2-2e2a463a3294" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306716 1145 "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the cyclist after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+2j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+2(i+2j) \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(10i+5j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the cyclist to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306718 13194139534737 true] [17592186306717 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534737 true] [17592186306717 1041 "field-1" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306717 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306718 13194139534737 true] [17592186306717 1110 #uuid "9fa755fc-69d3-5109-bb16-c586e912820a" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306718 1034 "5\\sqrt{5}" 13194139534737 true] [17592186306718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534737 true] [17592186306718 1111 #uuid "cd641dd4-97a3-5c4b-bde4-de798a18e5a5" 13194139534737 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-136375" 17592186306636 "q-136375/selectio